ice parking and prevent roadside parking on boulevards. Use turn lanes and monitor queues as demand grows.","repetition":"Translate copies by exactly 200 cells in x and/or y without rotation. Road portals: W/E y=100, N/S x=100, all six_lane_divided_road. Metro portals W/E y=104.75, double_subway_track. Ring and local streets remain inside each tile. No unique buildings are used.","transit":"Build the east-west metro at -20 metres; the line passes below surface roads. Underground station entrances face the south edge of the east-west boulevard at x=50 and x=150. Station footprints touch the modelled track edge. Four neighborhood bus stations anchor feeders through local spines and collectors to boulevard stops near the metro entrances. Run metro trains through adjacent tiles and feeder buses in both directions; bus and subway depots are provided elsewhere. Route lines and place ordinary roadside stops in game.","utilities":{"power":"Provided elsewhere: city generation and external transformer/substation capacity feed low-voltage cables in the connected roads. No generation or transformer is in this tile.","water":"Provided elsewhere: city pumping/treatment and trunk supply feed pipes under connected roads. No local pump or tower.","sewage":"Provided elsewhere: trunk sewers beneath connected roads lead to off-tile treatment. No local outlet or treatment plant.","garbage":"Provided elsewhere: off-tile recycling/incineration and their collection fleets serve all tile districts via collectors and boulevards. Assign collection coverage and scale processing and truck capacity with each copy."},"cityServices":"Bus/subway depots, road and park maintenance, postal sorting, prison and disaster warning are shared citywide outside the tile. Four local large shelters are included. Keep these external services assigned to every copied district.","capacity":"Zoned area is not a population or jobs estimate. Zone in phases against R/C/O demand. The geometric validator measures optimistic straight-line coverage, not road travel time, traffic performance, utility throughput or education/patient/vehicle adequacy. Watch actual enrollment, patient loads and queues; use unzoned reserves for added capacity.","reserves":"Unzoned gaps inside neighborhoods, the boulevard setback and the green outer seam are reserved open land, not catalog park assets or claimed service coverage."}}